# Content rules
- Each Topic needs: id (short, unique), icon, title, short, why, steps[], questions[].
- A Step has: title, body (HTML: <p>, <ul>, <table>, <code>, <div class="callout">), optional code, optional prompt.
- `prompt` = a realistic prompt the learner pastes into Cursor to practise the step.
- A Question has: q, lvl (1 basic | 2 mid | 3 senior), points (4-6 key points), a (model answer, 60-90 seconds spoken, first person).
- Append new questions at the end (ids are index-based and stored in localStorage).
- Register new topic arrays in src/data/index.ts and, if useful, in ROADMAP.
- Keep code examples short (< 35 lines) and correct for current library versions.

## Example
See src/data/topics/aws.ts for the reference format.
